WEBVTT

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.520
<i>My name is Kakeru Aizawa.</i>

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.400
<i>I'm a second year middle schooler.</i>

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.320
<i>My brother is a genius player in the</i>

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.400
<i>youth league, Suguru Aizawa.</i>

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:15.740
<i>I, the manager, was suddenly 
put into the selection match</i>

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:18.480
<i>and my brother kept sending 
me serious passes,</i>

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:23.160
<i>but, in the end, 
I couldn't score a single point.</i>

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.580
<i>My brother and Grey pointed 
out the weakness in my heart.</i>

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:29.130
<i>The next morning,</i>

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:31.540
<i>when I told him that 
I was quitting the club,</i>

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.070
<i>my brother talked to me about 
the "knight in the area"</i>

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.830
<i>that Japanese soccer is missing,</i>

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:38.460
<i>and the dream he had that day.</i>

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:42.250
<i>In that moment, I understood 
how my brother felt.</i>

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:43.800
<i>But in that instant...</i>

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:20.950
<b>A Brother's Pulse</b>

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:40.800
Brother?

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:47.180
Brother? Where are you going?

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.140
Hey, Brother...

00:03:11.430 --> 00:03:12.370
A 14 year old student, male.

00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:14.440
A metal pipe puncturing his chest.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.340
Respiration 24, heart rate 120.

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.480
The blood from his head won't stop.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:21.600
Seal it quickly.

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:23.040
One, two, three!

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:53.830
<b>Surgery in Progress</b>

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:57.330
Hey, wake up, Kakeru.

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.680
Oh, sorry, Brother.

00:04:06.410 --> 00:04:08.330
Aren't you going to become a regular?

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:09.270
C'mon!

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:10.960
Okay!

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.100
Doctor!

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:18.790
How are they?

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.530
My children are okay, right?

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.510
The younger brother's life is

00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:26.020
currently being maintained mechanically.

00:04:26.510 --> 00:04:29.710
The older brother's head injury 
was also quite serious.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:32.450
All right, next!

00:04:33.860 --> 00:04:34.620
Kakeru!

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:40.360
I did it!

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:42.010
Brother! I made it!

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.600
Hey! Everyone assemble for a second.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:56.350
Starting today we have a new member.

00:04:56.350 --> 00:04:59.180
A girl. Aren't you guys glad?

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.490
Um... hello. My name is Nana Mishima.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:07.420
Nice to meet you.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.150
You guys get along now.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.640
Okay!

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.450
Coach!

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:13.990
What's up, Suguru?

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.260
Her name... might be a problem.

00:05:17.260 --> 00:05:17.750
Hmm?

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.520
What?

00:05:19.830 --> 00:05:22.880
We already have a Mishima on our team,

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:25.010
and a Nanase.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:29.180
If someone said, "pass to Mishima,"

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.300
you wouldn't know which.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.770
Nana and Nanase are hard 
to tell apart, too.

00:05:33.010 --> 00:05:35.390
Hmm, that's true.

00:05:35.390 --> 00:05:36.830
What should we do?

00:05:36.830 --> 00:05:38.830
Do you have a nickname?

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:39.480
No.

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.170
Like, Mishi-man.

00:05:41.170 --> 00:05:42.100
That's exactly the same!

00:05:42.100 --> 00:05:44.060
What about Nanana Nana Nana?

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:45.450
That's too long, idiot.

00:05:45.910 --> 00:05:47.070
Seven...

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:49.410
What about Seven?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.030
Seven?

00:05:52.630 --> 00:05:55.160
"Seven" as a translation of "Nana." I get it.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:00.220
How about it?

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:01.290
Oh, okay.

00:06:06.430 --> 00:06:07.580
Seven...

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:22.830
Please be calm and listen.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.270
Sir, Ma'am,

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.560
we did everything we could,

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:30.240
but, regrettably, the older brother, Suguru-kun

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:33.360
was just determined to be brain dead.

00:06:33.760 --> 00:06:35.700
I'm terribly sorry.

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.590
Brain dead? He's brain dead?

00:06:39.240 --> 00:06:40.560
Unfortunately...

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:44.650
No!

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:46.890
Suguru...

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:52.850
Sir, Suguru-kun is an organ donor, correct?

00:06:55.430 --> 00:06:58.270
Suguru Aizawa
Kakeru Aizawa
Nana Mishima

00:06:58.590 --> 00:06:59.710
All right!

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:02.270
Th-There it is! There's my name!

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:04.230
We're both regulars now!

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.470
I'm getting anxious...

00:07:07.470 --> 00:07:09.700
I wonder if I'll be able to receive 
my brother's killer pass.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.490
You'll be fine.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:14.620
"My brother wouldn't send a pass 
that I couldn't get!" Right?

00:07:15.820 --> 00:07:16.620
Right.

00:07:17.040 --> 00:07:19.030
Time for practice.

00:07:19.030 --> 00:07:20.880
Wait up, Seven!

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:21.580
I'm coming, too.

00:07:29.670 --> 00:07:30.720
Seven!

00:07:34.750 --> 00:07:35.740
I'll crush you!

00:07:37.360 --> 00:07:38.520
Seven!

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:42.520
Go!

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:45.900
All right!

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.530
Nice goal, Kakeru.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:49.950
Nice, both of you.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:58.240
<b>Surgery in Progress</b>

00:08:13.390 --> 00:08:14.860
Hey, Kakeru.

00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:16.760
About today's second point...

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.850
Couldn't Seven have put that one in?

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:24.140
Yeah... But I hadn't scored 
since the last game,

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:25.520
so I was really happy.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:26.850
What are you saying?

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:28.360
We were leading.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:31.330
At times like that,
 the forward has to put it in.

00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.190
Right, Seven?

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:35.910
Seven?

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:38.960
Oh, right. Yeah.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:40.740
What's wrong?

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:42.580
You've been down since before the match.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:45.040
I'm completely fine.

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:46.860
Do you have a summer cold?

00:08:46.860 --> 00:08:49.000
The day after tomorrow is the semi-finals.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:51.290
I can't do a one top formation.

00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:52.550
I'll be fine.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:55.240
If it comes down to it, 
you can do it by yourself, Kakeru.

00:08:55.240 --> 00:08:57.930
What? Don't put this pressure on me.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:08:59.300
Sorry.

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.310
Keep it down back there!

00:09:01.530 --> 00:09:02.770
Oops!

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.070
I'm home!

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:07.940
I'm home!

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:10.480
Welcome back.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:11.770
The bath is ready.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:12.900
How was the match?

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:13.950
We won!

00:09:13.950 --> 00:09:16.260
Brother scored the first 
point and assisted one.

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:17.480
I scored the second point

00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.790
and Seven assisted one.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.530
If Seven assisted,

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:23.900
then Kake-nii, 
you had an easy point, right?

00:09:23.900 --> 00:09:26.040
Well spotted...

00:09:26.670 --> 00:09:28.570
But my point was...

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:30.240
Mom, Seven's mother came 
over last week, right?

00:09:30.240 --> 00:09:31.340
Oh, yes.

00:09:31.340 --> 00:09:32.690
What did she want?

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:34.640
Nothing in particular.

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:36.370
Are you hiding something?

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:41.290
You really are a sharp child, unlike Kakeru.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.150
Don't tell Kakeru.

00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:48.150
What?

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.860
That's not true, is it, Seven?

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:54.320
Sorry. It happened all of a sudden.

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.530
I'm leaving Japan tomorrow.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:00.990
That's so...

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:03.630
What are you looking like that for, Kakeru?

00:10:03.630 --> 00:10:05.450
You're the ace striker.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:09.070
From tomorrow onward, 
if you don't score, we'll lose!

00:10:09.070 --> 00:10:09.920
Right?

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:12.280
Tomorrow is a hat trick.

00:10:12.280 --> 00:10:13.630
It's a promise, Kakeru.

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:15.760
Right.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.940
Suguru-san, here.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.160
A good luck bracelet I made.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.860
There's two inside.

00:10:24.150 --> 00:10:24.970
Two?

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:27.940
One for you and one for Kakeru.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:31.100
They say that wishes come 
true when they break, right?

00:10:31.490 --> 00:10:34.400
I hope the three of us can 
play soccer again, someday...

00:10:37.810 --> 00:10:39.180
Oh, man.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.370
I told myself I definitely 
wouldn't cry today.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:42.810
Seven...

00:10:43.560 --> 00:10:46.850
"The three of us will wear 
the Japanese uniform."

00:10:46.850 --> 00:10:49.670
I'll never forget that promise.

00:10:51.020 --> 00:10:53.110
I made these bracelets while wishing

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.130
that someday our dream would come true.

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.010
Seven...

00:11:04.620 --> 00:11:08.060
I wonder if she's on a plane right now.

00:11:09.130 --> 00:11:10.200
Kakeru...

00:11:10.550 --> 00:11:12.540
What is it, Brother?

00:11:12.540 --> 00:11:14.940
Put this on.

00:11:15.820 --> 00:11:17.350
What's this?

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:18.500
Just put it on.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:19.900
Okay.

00:11:22.550 --> 00:11:26.310
Let's play so hard that these 
bracelets break in one match.

00:11:26.310 --> 00:11:26.990
All right?

00:11:26.990 --> 00:11:27.700
Right!

00:11:29.170 --> 00:11:31.250
Don't forget our promise to Seven.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:33.290
Let's take this hat trick!

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:34.430
Right!

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:58.610
Kakeru!

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.570
Auntie, Kakeru's...

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:05.530
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:08.990
Kakeru... thank goodness.

00:12:12.770 --> 00:12:14.020
<i>Seven...</i>

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:33.290
Kakeru...

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:45.780
<b>Kakeru Aizawa</b>

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.240
You're the girl who always 
comes and visits, right?

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.470
Ah, yes.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:50.820
I'm a childhood—

00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.210
I mean, I'm the soccer 
manager, Nana Mishima.

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:57.670
Just now, when he heard your voice,

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:01.380
his heart beat stronger in response.

00:13:09.110 --> 00:13:09.730
Hey...

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:10.320
Huh?

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:12.650
Which do you think it was

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:14.390
who responded to your voice?

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:21.510
Sorry...

00:13:21.510 --> 00:13:23.000
I've asked you something strange.

00:13:26.670 --> 00:13:30.220
Please come visit again, Mishima-san.

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.180
Yeah, he's much better now.

00:13:42.180 --> 00:13:45.380
The doctor was surprised he 
was recovering so quickly.

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:48.840
But he still doesn't know 
about Suguru-san, right?

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:51.650
I have no idea what to say.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:55.770
It won't do any good to worry about it.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:58.730
Let's just focus on getting him better.

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:04.650
Come in.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:07.070
Kakeru! We've come to—

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:11.080
I was so worried, Kakeru!

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:12.620
Ow...

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.230
You little...

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:20.420
We heard it was serious heart surgery,
 so we were worried.

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:21.630
You seem healthy.

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:24.710
Yeah, I don't have any 
other serious injuries,

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.260
so I should be released soon.

00:14:26.530 --> 00:14:29.150
Get better and come back to the club.

00:14:29.150 --> 00:14:30.260
That's right.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:32.350
Didn't you hear?

00:14:32.350 --> 00:14:34.720
I'm quitting the soccer club.

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.570
What?

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.590
Hold on a second, Kakeru.

00:14:37.590 --> 00:14:39.210
What are you saying, all of a sudden?

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:43.250
If you say something like 
that, Suguru-san will...

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:47.540
I've already talked to 
my brother about it.

00:14:47.540 --> 00:14:50.160
I assumed you all already knew.

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:56.790
You know, I'd like to talk it over 
with my brother one more time.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:14:59.390
It's a pretty big decision

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:01.290
and I'm worried I didn't 
explain myself well.

00:15:02.870 --> 00:15:04.710
I want to see my brother soon.

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:06.600
Kakeru...

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:09.130
What's wrong, Seven?

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.130
You're acting weird.

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:13.600
I'll talk to him

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.200
about his brother.

00:15:15.550 --> 00:15:16.780
You're...

00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:22.920
Nice to meet you, Kakeru Aizawa-kun.

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:25.020
I'm the clinical psychiatrist, Ayaka Mine.

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:27.710
Nice... to meet you.

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:33.950
I was Suguru-san's counselor 
at this hospital.

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:39.610
Kakeru-kun,

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:42.560
can you remain calm and listen?

00:15:43.760 --> 00:15:44.790
Yeah...

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:46.500
Doctor!

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:52.430
Kakeru-kun,

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:56.390
Your brother, Suguru-san...

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:02.810
...died in that accident.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:19.220
You're joking, right?

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:23.750
Unfortunately, it's the truth.

00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:27.290
Seven, what is she talking about?

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:32.150
I'm sorry... I'm so sorry, Kakeru.

00:16:33.400 --> 00:16:35.060
Wait a second...

00:16:35.060 --> 00:16:36.510
What's wrong with all of you?

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.150
My brother...

00:16:38.150 --> 00:16:38.930
My brother...

00:16:39.150 --> 00:16:40.260
Where is he?

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:42.150
Hey, Kakeru.

00:16:44.520 --> 00:16:45.350
Brother!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:47.310
Brother!

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:07.600
Are you planning on wasting the life

00:17:07.600 --> 00:17:09.340
that your brother gave you?

00:17:33.770 --> 00:17:34.740
Doctor,

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.790
should we tell Kakeru about the transplant?

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:40.700
From my point of view, 
I cannot recommend it.

00:17:41.490 --> 00:17:47.090
We cannot predict how Kakeru 
will react to the news.

00:17:47.090 --> 00:17:50.170
We should prepare for the worst case.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:51.510
That's true...

00:17:51.800 --> 00:17:53.940
Kakeru is alive because of the heart

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.130
transplanted from his beloved brother.

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:59.100
<i>Suguru-san's heart...</i>

00:18:00.270 --> 00:18:02.020
<i>was transplanted into Kakeru?!</i>

00:18:05.520 --> 00:18:07.520
<b>Two Months Later</b>

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:12.810
Tour de France!

00:18:14.840 --> 00:18:16.140
You seem energetic.

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.570
Oh, Dr. Mine.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:21.030
I feel better than before the accident.

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.750
You're being discharged tomorrow,

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:29.210
so don't overwork yourself.

00:18:29.510 --> 00:18:30.920
I'm fine!

00:18:30.920 --> 00:18:33.170
I feel restless, if I don't move around.

00:18:36.830 --> 00:18:39.230
How is Kakeru Aizawa-kun?

00:18:39.230 --> 00:18:41.460
He is mentally stable

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:43.480
and his physical recovery 
is progressing smoothly.

00:18:43.480 --> 00:18:46.560
Stress injury is no longer a concern.

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:47.720
I see...

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:50.910
Even with the donor and 
recipient being brothers,

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:53.520
this degree of adaptation to a 
foreign organ is surprising.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:58.280
At this rate, further 
complications are unlikely.

00:18:58.500 --> 00:18:59.280
Yes.

00:19:09.180 --> 00:19:11.050
Be careful of cars!

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:11.580
Okay.

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:13.650
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:19:13.650 --> 00:19:15.190
If you're tired, rest right away.

00:19:15.190 --> 00:19:16.190
I know.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:17.650
Don't get lost.

00:19:17.650 --> 00:19:18.300
Okay.

00:19:19.760 --> 00:19:23.120
I'm fine without everyone sending me off.

00:19:23.680 --> 00:19:24.810
I'm heading out.

00:19:25.980 --> 00:19:27.810
Everyone,

00:19:28.080 --> 00:19:29.760
I'm sorry I made you all worry,

00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:31.870
but, as you can see, 
I've fully recovered.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.150
Hurray!

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:35.120
Congratulations on your recovery!

00:19:33.930 --> 00:19:39.110
Hurray! Hurray!

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:37.390
I'm so glad, Aizawa-kun!

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:45.080
Are you sure,

00:19:45.080 --> 00:19:47.540
Club Resignation

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:46.140
Kakeru?

00:19:47.960 --> 00:19:50.490
I apologize, Kunimatsu-senpai.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.620
I was seriously injured

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:55.500
and I'm not sure I really want 
to continue as manager.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:57.560
I understand.

00:19:58.570 --> 00:20:00.010
I'll hold onto this.

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:05.470
Your brother...

00:20:06.110 --> 00:20:09.270
was going to become a world 
soccer player for Japan.

00:20:10.630 --> 00:20:11.440
It's such a shame.

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:12.970
Yes.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:14.320
Kakeru,

00:20:14.740 --> 00:20:16.520
come back to the soccer club 
whenever you feel like it.

00:20:17.130 --> 00:20:19.400
But not as a manager.

00:20:20.250 --> 00:20:21.510
Come as a player...

00:20:21.510 --> 00:20:22.860
as a striker.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.510
Thanks for everything.

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:31.960
Okay, pass.

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:34.950
One more.

00:20:48.950 --> 00:20:49.850
Kakeru...

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:52.940
I heard from Mishima-san,

00:20:52.940 --> 00:20:54.820
you're physically recovered, right?

00:20:54.820 --> 00:20:56.770
You can even handle strenuous exercise.

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:00.700
Even if it isn't possible now,

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:01.690
at least by summer—

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:04.250
Yuusuke, give me a break.

00:21:04.250 --> 00:21:05.660
I've quit soccer.

00:21:05.880 --> 00:21:07.120
Are you running away?

00:21:09.240 --> 00:21:10.830
<i>Always running away...</i>

00:21:11.380 --> 00:21:13.170
<i>That's why you ran away 
to the manager's position.</i>

00:21:13.170 --> 00:21:14.830
<i>Am I wrong, Kakeru?</i>

00:21:14.830 --> 00:21:19.000
<i>What does someone who just 
runs away know about me?</i>

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.430
Forget it. Pass the ball.

00:21:26.800 --> 00:21:28.230
That's not it.

00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:31.890
I'm not running away.

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:42.860
Yuusuke-kun,

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.830
Is Kakeru really quitting?

00:21:46.600 --> 00:21:47.660
I couldn't move.

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:52.350
Like when I was matched up with Suguru-san,

00:21:52.350 --> 00:21:54.010
I felt like if I tried to approach him,

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:55.660
something might happen.

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.070
What about practice?

00:22:02.070 --> 00:22:03.230
I'm taking today off.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:04.890
Where are you headed?

00:22:04.890 --> 00:22:06.070
The hospital.

00:22:06.070 --> 00:22:08.300
Then maybe I'll tag along.

00:22:10.460 --> 00:22:13.000
The soccer club is having a hard time.

00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:15.230
Without Suguru-san...

00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:16.790
Is that so?

00:22:17.560 --> 00:22:19.190
Everyone's head is somewhere else.

00:22:19.530 --> 00:22:21.310
No one can concentrate on practice,

00:22:21.840 --> 00:22:25.610
and most of the female managers who 
had their eyes on Suguru-san quit.

00:22:27.200 --> 00:22:28.070
What about you?

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:29.480
What?

00:22:29.480 --> 00:22:33.540
Will you quit the team because 
my brother is gone, too?

00:22:34.280 --> 00:22:37.020
No, I won't quit.

00:22:41.180 --> 00:22:43.500
It sure was fun...

00:22:43.810 --> 00:22:45.690
Suguru-san was the conductor

00:22:46.020 --> 00:22:48.050
and Seven and I were on the two forwards.

00:22:48.730 --> 00:22:51.370
Say, after I left for America,

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:52.960
how did the tournament go?

00:22:53.520 --> 00:22:54.620
We took the championship.

00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:55.600
Really?

00:22:55.600 --> 00:22:57.430
And the hat trick as well.

00:22:58.420 --> 00:23:01.820
You kept your promise to me.

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:03.400
Yeah.

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:07.040
Wait up!

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:11.390
I had a hard time understanding 
my brother recently.

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:12.930
Kakeru...

00:23:14.550 --> 00:23:16.230
He must have been tired

00:23:16.230 --> 00:23:18.500
of having such a useless brother.

00:23:19.320 --> 00:23:22.760
I think he couldn't forgive me for holding on

00:23:22.760 --> 00:23:24.090
halfheartedly to soccer.

00:23:24.220 --> 00:23:25.580
That's not true!

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:27.500
Suguru-san's definitely not like that.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:28.430
Hey, Kakeru!

00:23:28.430 --> 00:23:29.640
You don't really think—

00:23:29.640 --> 00:23:32.540
Mister! Can you get our ball?

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:39.100
Mister!

00:24:03.430 --> 00:24:03.950
What the—

00:24:38.590 --> 00:24:41.340
Suguru-san?

00:24:45.940 --> 00:25:15.340
<b>Next time: Last Pass</b>

00:24:47.770 --> 00:24:51.610
Alive because of a heart 
transplant from his brother,

00:24:52.440 --> 00:24:56.480
Kakeru, unable to accept reality,
 stops moving forward.

00:24:57.050 --> 00:24:59.200
The family, who can do 
nothing but watch,

00:24:59.200 --> 00:25:01.320
and his rivals.

00:25:01.880 --> 00:25:05.180
The emotions that he finds 
in his brother's diary

00:25:05.180 --> 00:25:07.230
and the answer he gives to Nana...

00:25:07.420 --> 00:25:09.180
Next time on The Knight in the Area:

00:25:09.180 --> 00:25:11.430
the fourth episode, "Last Pass."

00:25:11.800 --> 00:25:13.490
Accept it, Kakeru!
